# ══ THE CONTENT SECURITY POLICY — L31 v2.1b+c, S5b ════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Shipped in the SAME COMMIT as the in-app chat, because the chat is what makes it load-bearing:
# from S5b the Ask dock renders MODEL-AUTHORED text on an origin whose localStorage holds an OpenAI
# key. The policy cannot stop exfiltration to OpenAI — `connect-src` has to allow that host for the
# feature to exist — but it stops exfiltration to an ATTACKER's host, which is the whole payoff of
# an XSS here. (opus-plan-review-2.md §G.2, kickoff RC11.)
#
# ⚠️ THIS FILE IS NOT THE ONLY PLACE THE POLICY IS SET. `functions/_middleware.js` applies the same
# string to every `text/html` response it returns, because `_headers` is documented as applying to
# STATIC ASSET responses and every non-excluded path on this project goes through a Pages Function
# (`public/_routes.json` includes `/*`). Rather than deploy and find out, both are shipped and a
# unit test asserts the two strings are byte-identical. The live host is asserted after the deploy.
#
# ── EVERY DIRECTIVE, AND WHY IT HAS THE VALUE IT HAS (all MEASURED against `dist/`) ────────────
#
#   default-src 'self'      the floor. Anything not named below falls here.
#   connect-src             'self' for the atlas, the chunks, the dictionaries, /api/timing;
#                           api.openai.com for the chat, and NOTHING else. This single line is what
#                           makes an injected script unable to POST the key anywhere useful.
#   script-src 'self'       MEASURED: `dist/index.html` and `dist/v2/index.html` each carry exactly
#                           one `<script type="module" crossorigin src="/assets/…">` and zero inline
#                           scripts, so no 'unsafe-inline' and no hash is needed.
#   style-src 'self'        MEASURED: zero `<style>` blocks and zero `style="` attributes in the
#                           built HTML. React's `style={{…}}` writes through the CSSOM
#                           (`node.style.prop = …`), which CSP does not govern — `style-src-attr`
#                           covers style ATTRIBUTES, not property assignment. So 'unsafe-inline' is
#                           NOT included, which is what RC11 asks for ("prefer no 'unsafe-inline'").
#                           The sweep asserts zero `securitypolicyviolation` events at every
#                           viewport, because this reasoning is the one that could be wrong.
#   img-src 'self' data: blob:   the snapshot path: `toDataURL` plates and canvas blobs.
#   font-src 'self'         the CJK stack is self-hosted; no font CDN.
#   object-src 'none'       no plugins, ever.
#   base-uri 'none'         an injected <base> can redirect every relative URL on the page.
#   frame-ancestors 'none'  MEASURED SAFE FOR THE WIDGET: the Apps-SDK widget is delivered INLINE in
#                           the MCP resource body (`functions/mcp.js` — `contents: [{uri, mimeType:
#                           'text/html+skybridge', text: WIDGET_HTML}]`), so ChatGPT renders it in
#                           its OWN sandbox and never frames a document from this origin. Nothing
#                           on this origin is meant to be framed, so this is 'none' site-wide
#                           rather than scoped per path.
#   form-action 'none'      there is no form that posts anywhere; an injected one now cannot.
#
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://api.openai.com; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
